<section class="section prose-grid"><h2>Curation with<br/>a sense of discovery.</h2><div><p>Each run introduces six games. Keep a discovery or crush it and move on, then review your collection back at camp. Different routes make room for popular releases, cult favorites, and less familiar work.</p><p>The experiment brings together interface design, human curation, and AI-assisted product development. It established the independent practice that later expanded into authored games and their development infrastructure.</p><dl class="facts"><div><dt>Release</dt><dd>Windows · February 2026</dd></div><div><dt>Stack</dt><dd>Python / FastAPI / JavaScript</dd></div><div><dt>Focus</dt><dd>Discovery & curation</dd></div></dl></div></section><div class="gallery"><img src="/images/torch-2.jpeg" alt="The Gem Cave displaying three saved game discoveries" loading="lazy"/><img src="/images/torch-3.png" alt="A discovered horror game with Keep and Crush controls and Danny the mole" loading="lazy"/></div><section class="section archive-strip"><div><h2>The next chapter</h2><p>From exploring other people’s horror games to building a haunted house of our own.</p></div><a class="text-link" href="/games/a-household-exorcism/">A Household Exorcism →</a></section></Portfolio>
